        directAnswer: "A crypto exchange fee schedule should be read as an operating checklist, not a single headline rate. OKX, Kraken, Gate, MEXC and Bitget all publish official fee pages, but each page organizes cost information around different product surfaces, account tiers, market types or VIP rules. The decision outcome is to map the exact trade type, maker or taker role, funding or withdrawal path, discount rule, eligibility tier, and date of the fee page before comparing two venues. A user who cannot identify the product surface or the current tier should treat the comparison as incomplete rather than assuming the lowest visible rate applies.",
