        directAnswer: "DTCC's tokenization materials are useful because they separate tokenized representation from the official post-trade record. DTCC Learning says tokenized securities processed through the Tokenization Service remain recorded in DTC's official books and records, and that tokenized collateral can move high-quality assets in near real time across borders and time zones under appropriate market arrangements. DTCC's Digital Assets page frames DTC-held securities as assets that can be represented digitally across approved networks while remaining anchored to existing protections and resiliency. The decision outcome is to map the recordkeeper, network approval, collateral-use case, settlement link, asset-servicing path, and what does not transfer merely because a digital representation exists.",
