        directAnswer: "NexuAlpha Radar treats self-trade prevention as an order-reconciliation problem, not as a generic market-integrity badge. Binance Spot API glossary defines Self Trade Prevention as preventing a user's orders, or a tradeGroupId's orders, from matching against their own and exposes fields such as preventedQuantity and preventedMatchId for STP events. OKX API documentation says mandatory self-trade prevention applies at master-account level across the master account and affiliated sub-accounts, with cancel_maker, cancel_taker and cancel_both modes. OKX also says user orders can be canceled by the system for self-trade prevention and users can refer to cancelSource. The radar score asks whether a bot can capture the mode, affected order, prevented quantity, cancellation reason and downstream position or balance reconciliation without double-counting liquidity.",
