        directAnswer: "DTCC Tokenization Service should be read as market-infrastructure plumbing with explicit control assumptions, not as a generic claim that any tokenized security can circulate freely. DTCC says tokenized DTC assets can move between traditional and blockchain ecosystems using the same CUSIP across approved networks, while preserving the same legal rights, economic interest and investor protections associated with the underlying securities. DTCC also describes embedded controls such as mint, burn, pause and clawback functionality and near real-time ownership tracking through ComposerX LedgerScan. SEC Crypto@SEC materials keep tokenized-security analysis tied to rights, records and federal-securities-law treatment. The decision is to verify asset eligibility, network approval, official record source, lifecycle controls and participant scope before treating a tokenized DTC asset as operationally ready.",
