        directAnswer: "Coinbase publishes three different address-governance surfaces that should not be merged into one generic withdrawal-safety claim. Coinbase Exchange whitelisting restricts withdrawals to Address Book entries, gives an initial 8-hour window, then applies 48-hour holds for new addresses and disabling whitelisting. Coinbase Prime Trusted Address Book Protection is automatically enabled for portfolios and routes updates through consensus approvals. Coinbase Prime Onchain Wallet has a separate Onchain Trusted Address Book where Destination Protection is active by default and changes are governed by the General Consensus setting. The decision is which wallet, account type and approval model controls a transfer before any funds move.",
