        directAnswer: "Binance published a Spot API update notice on June 25, 2026 for an infrastructure upgrade scheduled for July 9, 2026 at 07:00 UTC with an expected one-hour duration. The action item was narrow: during the update window, WebSocket connections may be disconnected and users should reconnect to restore the connection. The current developer documentation adds the operational context: cancelReplace exists for REST and WebSocket order flows, REST cancelReplace is signed, filters and order counts are evaluated before processing, and orderRateLimitExceededMode can change whether cancellation is still attempted when unfilled order limits are exceeded. A safe operational checklist therefore verifies connection recovery, subscription replay, private order-state reconciliation, rate-limit handling and secret-free logs before calling the update a non-event.",
