        llmsExcerpt: "Binance and Kraken expose different order-failover controls, so the comparison should start with the failure mode rather than the brand. Binance documents cancelReplace for REST and WebSocket order flows, evaluates filters and order counts before cancellation and replacement, and supports orderRateLimitExceededMode values that change whether cancellation is still attempted when unfilled order limits are exceeded. Binance also announced a Spot API infrastructure upgrade where WebSocket connections could disconnect and users should reconnect. Kraken Futures documents a dead man switch endpoint that cancels all user orders when a timeout expires unless the user keeps extending or disables the timer. The practical decision is to separate replace logic, cancel-only behavior, connection recovery, timer refresh cadence, API authentication, and private order-state reconciliation before automating either venue."
