        directAnswer: "NexuAlpha's collateral radar treats alert delivery, platform caps and liquidation formulas as separate evidence fields. Bybit's platform collateral-limit page says yellow and red warning icons and notifications can appear as collateral usage approaches or reaches a platform limit, but it also tells users not to rely solely on system notifications. Bybit's Crypto Loans FAQ says margin-call and liquidation thresholds can trigger email, SMS and push alerts, while warning that risk alerts may be delayed or experience glitches. OKX describes a separate platform-wide collateralized borrowing limit whose impact depends on account mode and borrowing state. A useful radar therefore records five fields for every venue: trigger, user-visible alert, machine-readable check, transfer or borrow restriction, and liquidation or repayment action.",
