        directAnswer: "The SEC's September 25, 2026 crypto-asset FAQ is useful only if users keep its status and scope narrow. The Division of Corporation Finance says the answers are staff views, not a rule, regulation or SEC statement, and they have no legal force or effect. The FAQ addresses questions related to the Commission's March 17, 2026 interpretive release. For functionality and decentralization, the FAQ emphasizes that whether an issuer has fulfilled represented essential managerial efforts depends on how the issuer defined or described functionality or decentralization, not a general market conception. The March interpretive release separately classifies crypto assets by characteristics, uses and functions and states that a non-security crypto asset can still be offered and sold subject to an investment contract. The decision outcome is to map issuer promises, current network facts, offer context and staff-guidance status before treating a token classification as settled.",
