        directAnswer: "Binance's CAAS FAQ turns subaccount operations into an entity, KYC and endpoint-routing problem. Binance says Travel Rule requirements depend on the entity a subaccount is tagged to, AU-tagged accounts require questionnaires for deposits and withdrawals with no minimum threshold, and IN-tagged accounts apply Travel Rule above a 1,000 USD threshold. It also says non-Travel-Rule entities should keep using the capital withdrawal endpoint, while tagged entities should migrate to the localentity withdrawal endpoint. For KYC restrictions, newly created non-KYC subaccounts cannot create API keys or retrieve deposit addresses, deposits into older non-KYC subaccounts can be rejected, and non-KYC subaccounts face trading and transfer limits. The safe user outcome is to map entity tag, KYC state, endpoint, API key owner and recovery path before treating a subaccount as operational.",
