        directAnswer: "NexuAlpha's subaccount radar treats KYC state, API scope and governance as separate evidence fields. Binance's CAAS FAQ makes KYC and entity tagging material to deposit addresses, API-key creation, Travel Rule routing and transfers. OKX Help makes subaccount setup, account mode, API permissions, passphrase and trusted-IP restriction material to bot or external-platform use. Kraken Organizations adds a different layer: API keys are not members, governed operations create requests, keys cannot approve, and the key secret is shown once. A useful disclosure radar must therefore ask four questions for every venue: what account object is being controlled, what KYC or entity gate applies, which permission can move value, and whether automation can complete the action or only start a human-governed request.",
