        directAnswer: "A safe Gemini onboarding flow separates identity verification, sign-in authentication and withdrawal-destination control. Gemini says completing registration requires uploading a clear full photo ID in the app and enables full trading and transfer capabilities after verification. Gemini says 2FA is required and cannot be disabled, and its passkeys article says opting into passkeys makes them the default 2FA method across web and mobile for sign-ins and withdrawals. For destination control, Gemini's Address Book page says known external addresses can be stored by asset and Withdrawal Protection may impose a 7-day wait for newly added addresses on single-user accounts, while multi-user accounts use administrator or manager approval. For EU/EEA and UK approved-address flows, Gemini says a wallet address cannot be used until it clears the waiting period or multi-user approval. The tutorial is security setup, not a referral or deposit instruction.",
