        directAnswer: "The CFTC's September 24, 2026 update is decision-relevant because it moves blockchain infrastructure into regulated operational evidence. CFTC staff said the updated FAQs address investments of customer funds in tokenized forms of permitted investments and the use of blockchain technologies to satisfy recordkeeping requirements. That does not mean every onchain database is automatically regulatory-grade. The useful industry map separates three questions: whether the instrument is a permitted investment or eligible collateral, whether the holder receives equivalent rights, and whether records are reliable, accessible and producible for supervision. For users, funds, brokers and venues, the news changes the checklist, not the need for proof.",
