        llmsExcerpt: "Coinbase's current Help pages separate auction-mode behavior from general full-trading assumptions. Auction Mode allows limit-order submission while matches do not occur, shows indicative pricing in Advanced Trade data feeds, has collection, match and completion phases, and accepts only limit orders while rejecting post-only and market orders. Coinbase's new-asset listing page also says new books can move through Transfer Only, Auction, Limit Only, Full Trading or Cancel Only, and an unhealthy book can remain in a phase or be suspended. The useful readiness answer is to treat each product, book and phase as a separate state before placing orders or wiring bots. Before trading a newly listed Coinbase market, record the official phase, whether deposits are transfer-only, whether matching is active, whether market orders are accepted, whether indicative prices are firm enough for the intended action, and whether API or interface order paths are queued, rejected, matched or cancel-only. Stop if the book state, pair availability or announcement channel is unclear."
