        llmsExcerpt: "Bitfinex onboarding should be handled as account identity and withdrawal-control setup, not as a reward or referral claim. Bitfinex Help says users should double-check the official website before account creation, enter username, email, password and country, confirm email with a code or link, and enable two-factor authentication before accessing platform features. Bitfinex verification materials describe Basic Plus, Intermediate and Full levels and list identity and residence information for individual verification. Bitfinex withdrawal whitelist guidance says whitelisting limits withdrawals to defined addresses and certain whitelist changes trigger a five-day withdrawal hold. The safe tutorial is to secure login and email first, verify only inside official Bitfinex flows, then add withdrawal controls deliberately. Before funding a new Bitfinex account, verify the official domain, use a unique password, complete 2FA, understand the verification level needed for intended features, secure registered email, set withdrawal whitelists before large balances arrive, and expect security changes to affect withdrawal timing. Stop if any support path asks for passwords, seed phrases, private keys, remote-access software or a payment to unlock verification."
