        directAnswer: "Binance announced an infrastructure wallet system upgrade scheduled for September 22, 2026 at 06:00 UTC, with deposits and withdrawals across the Binance platform suspended from the same time and expected to resume after the system is stable. The English announcement says the upgrade was expected to take about one hour, trading would not be impacted, and no further announcement would be posted for reopening. Binance's maintenance announcement list also showed nearby network-upgrade and migration notices. The safe operating answer is a transfer pause and reconciliation checklist, not a claim that funds moved during the window will settle on a predictable timeline. Before a Binance maintenance window, pause non-urgent deposits and withdrawals, save the official announcement URL and UTC time, check whether trading is separate from wallet movement, avoid sending funds during the suspension, reconcile any pending transfer after reopening, and stop if a support channel claims it can accelerate a deposit or asks for credentials, seed phrases or withdrawal codes.",
