        directAnswer: "Deribit registration is an account-opening and verification workflow, not a reward claim. Deribit Support says users register through the production Deribit website, choose email, Google or Apple, confirm email, enable mandatory two-factor authentication, and complete Know Your Customer verification. Deribit also says users should use the production environment for real accounts, check restricted jurisdictions, log in with registered email, and treat client secrets like passwords. The safe path is to verify the official domain, secure 2FA before funding and stop if any non-official channel asks for identity documents or credentials. Before funding a new Deribit account, verify the production domain, confirm the country is supported, use a unique email and password, enable 2FA or passkey/security-key protection, complete KYC only through the official account area, test login recovery without exposing secrets, and make the first deposit only after account status, withdrawal controls and device security are clear.",
