        llmsExcerpt: "Travel Rule disclosures change the deposit and withdrawal path differently across venues and regions. Binance says VASPs may need originator and beneficiary names and wallet addresses, with questionnaires and possible self-hosted-wallet control tests. OKX Europe says regulated-region users may need beneficiary legal names, private-wallet status and wallet ownership verification. Coinbase Europe and Kraken regional guidance similarly frame extra counterparty information as jurisdiction-dependent. The radar output is a data-minimization and stop-rule checklist. Before moving funds across a regulated exchange boundary, record the jurisdiction, counterparty type, legal-name spelling, wallet ownership evidence, VASP selection, unsupported-route condition, deposit-lock condition and privacy boundary. Stop if a venue asks for information through a non-official channel, if the sender cannot provide required originator details, or if the route requires exposing private keys or seed phrases."
