        directAnswer: "DTCC describes its Tokenization Service as market infrastructure for tokenized DTC-custodied assets, with DTC-issued tokens designed to represent the same legal rights, economic interest and investor protections as underlying securities. Public material also points to eligible networks and participant wallet registration. The decision question is not whether tokenization is novel; it is whether the network, wallet and official entitlement controls are production-ready for a specific participant. Before relying on DTC tokenized assets operationally, map participant eligibility, wallet registration, supported network, same-CUSIP handling, ownership-right continuity, corporate-action processing, mint/burn/pause/clawback controls, reconciliation and the fallback path when a chain or wallet route is unavailable.",
