        directAnswer: "DTC's tokenization service and the SEC's Tokenized Securities Venue framework address different market functions. DTC is developing infrastructure for eligible securities records, registered wallets and lifecycle processing within regulated post-trade systems. A TSV under the SEC's temporary exemption is a permissioned trading venue using automated market maker liquidity pools for tokenized NMS stocks. Institutions must map issuance, ownership record, custody, trading, price formation, clearing, settlement, corporate actions and trading halts separately rather than treating either label as an end-to-end market stack.",
