        directAnswer: "OKX deprecated order-book checksum validation for the books, books-l2-tbt and books50-l2-tbt JSON WebSocket channels in production on June 23, 2026. The checksum field remains present but is fixed to zero and must not be used for integrity checks; clients should validate continuity with seqId and prevSeqId. A robust consumer must treat a broken sequence link as a state-loss event, discard the suspect local book, obtain a fresh snapshot and resume only after the new sequence chain is coherent.",
