        directAnswer: "Coinbase staked ETH and Lido stETH both provide exposure to Ethereum staking, but they create different control surfaces. Coinbase uses an eligible custodial account and offers standard unstaking, sometimes an instant paid route, and cbETH wrapping where available. Lido issues a transferable liquid-staking token controlled through smart contracts and a FIFO withdrawal-request, finalization and claim process, with secondary-market exits outside the protocol. The useful choice depends on jurisdiction, custody preference, token and smart-contract risk, conversion rate, exit route, fees, queue state, tax treatment and the user's ability to operate a self-custody wallet safely.",
