        llmsExcerpt: "On August 12, 2026, SEC investment-management staff issued a fact-specific no-action response concerning affiliated funds investing in the Franklin OnChain U.S. Government Money Fund and the custody framework under Section 17(f) and Rule 17f-2. The incoming request describes official share records maintained through an integrated recordkeeping system, book-entry ownership and independent-accountant reconciliation and verification. The response is not a general regulatory approval for every tokenized fund or blockchain custody design; each product still requires its own legal entity, authoritative record, transfer, redemption, custody and exception-handling analysis."
