        directAnswer: "A stablecoin and a tokenized bank deposit can both move on programmable infrastructure, but they are not the same claim. A tokenized deposit is generally a digital representation of a deposit liability on a bank balance sheet, while a stablecoin is typically a claim under an issuer's reserve, redemption and legal structure. Users should compare the obligor, par-conversion right, reserve or balance-sheet backing, settlement asset, transfer rule, insolvency treatment and operating hours before treating either token as cash-equivalent.",
